  triage:correctionNote "2026-07-26 (quality-mgr): independently re-verified at integrate/phase-AI tip against arch-ctm's legacy close/waive batch recommendation -- initially declined close, still OPEN: scripts/test_atm_graft_python.py:43,45,47 still hardcodes 'omega-prime'/'hermes' inline with no comment. Confirmed via direct file read, not self-report." ;
  triage:closureNote "2026-07-27 (quality-mgr): superseding the correctionNote above with a real closure after arch-ctm's follow-up correction. Independently checked the actual enforcement mechanism this finding cites (RULE-008/009 via .just/check_test_identity_literals.py, config at .just/lint-config.toml [identities]): forbidden_literals is team-lead/arch-ctm/arch-qa/arch-inj/arch-obs/quality-mgr/publisher/atm-dev -- neither 'omega-prime' nor 'hermes' appears, and the lint only scans workspace Rust files (iter_workspace_rust_files) while the flagged file is scripts/test_atm_graft_python.py, a Python script outside the lint's scope entirely. The finding's title claims these are 'production-significant' literals, but no production-canonical mapping or forbidden-literal entry exists for either string, and 'hermes'/'omega-prime' are established example identities used throughout this repo's own docs/fixtures (see also RSH tracker precedent). Closing as invalid: the original 'production-significant' premise does not hold against the actual configured rule, independently confirmed against the lint config and code, not merely asserted by arch-ctm." .

